<title>LEBANON: Lebanese airline workers to strike on Tuesday.</title>
<headline>Lebanese airline workers to strike on Tuesday.</headline>
<dateline>BEIRUT 1997-01-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Employees of Lebanon's national carrier Middle East Airlines will stage a 24-hour strike on Tuesday to protest against the company's refusal to meet their pay demands, the Lebanese Pilots' Union said on Friday.</p>
<p>The union said in a statement that MEA's 200 pilots and 3,500 ground crew will strike from midnight on Monday until midnight on Tuesday.</p>
<p>It was not immediately known how many MEA flights would be affected by the stoppage. Arab and international airlines will continue to operate their flights to and from Beirut airport normally, airport sources said.</p>
<p>- Beirut editorial (961 1) 602057 745307 745308</p>
</text>
